rooms_desc ({"This is Smeghead's house......can't you tell??It is unbelievably luxurious, so much so, that you can't help butstare around in amazement. This is the lounge/entertainment roomwhere parties are held. In one corner is the biggest entertainmentcentre you've seen, complete with a 61-cm colour TV (with surroundsound), video and mutlidisc CD player. In another corner you see hispersonal computer setup, which is a P100 with all the extras and add-onsyou ever heard of, and along the opposite wall is a fully stocked wetbar, with all the alcholic beverages you ever heard of, plus a few exotic one thrwon in for good measure.","This is Smeghead's bedroom. In the centre of the room is a king-sizedheated waterbed. Along one wall is the bigget walk-in wardrobe you haveever seen. There is a large stereo setup on the bedside table, but it palesinto insignificance compared to the setup in the lounge room.The walls are covered in posters from all the latest movies, and ofbands like Guns'n'Roses and Metallica.","This is the bathroom. As you look around in awe and wonder you can'thelp but notice the absoluely HUGE sunken hot tub in the centre of thefloor. It looks big enough for about 10-15 people, more if they wereREALLY good friends..... You also notice the shower stall in one corner, used for when Smeghead can't be bothered taking the time to run thespa and whirlpool built into the tub.","This is Smeghead's kitchen. This is where Smeghead eats if he can'tbe botherered calling Pizza Hut home delivery. In one corner is thebiggest fridge/freezer unit you have ever seen, while in the centre ofthe room is an elegant table setting for when Smeghead either eats athome or invites friends over for dinner.Along one wall is the cupboards, stuffed with food and cutlery, the likesof which you have never seen before.","This is the front yard of Smeghead's house. It is absolutely HUGE!!You can see a rugby field, a swimming pool (olympic sized), a tennis courtand various other sporting facilities scattered all over the lawn.There is also a quiet-looking grove of trees along one fence whereSmeghead goes when he wants some peace and quiet.",0,0,0,0,0,})
